CROSS-EXAMINATION TRANSCRIPT - KEY EXCERPTS

VICTIM (Prosecution Witness):

Q: You stated that you were raped on 10.05.2025.
A: Yes.

Q: Why did you not inform the police immediately?
A: I was scared and ashamed.

Q: Did you inform your parents immediately?
A: No, I informed them after two days.

Q: You were in a relationship with the accused for six months.
A: Yes, but he promised to marry me.

Q: Did you have consensual relations with him before?
A: Yes, but only because he promised marriage.

Q: Did you ever refuse his advances before?
A: No, I never refused.

Q: Did you raise any alarm during the alleged incident?
A: No, I was in shock.

Q: Did you have any injuries when you went for medical examination?
A: No major injuries.

FRIEND (Prosecution Witness):

Q: You are a close friend of the victim.
A: Yes.

Q: When did the victim inform you about the incident?
A: On 11.05.2025.

Q: Did she tell you she was raped?
A: She said the accused forced himself on her.

Q: Did she mention any threat or force?
A: She said he forced her.

Q: Did you see any marks on her body?
A: No, she looked normal.

Q: Did she tell you why she delayed reporting?
A: She said she was scared.

ACCUSED (Defence Witness):

Q: You had a relationship with the victim.
A: Yes, we were in a relationship.

Q: Was it consensual?
A: Yes, completely consensual.

Q: Did you promise to marry her?
A: Yes, I did promise marriage.

Q: Did you refuse to marry later?
A: I said I needed time due to family circumstances.

Q: Did you ever force her?
A: Never, never forced her.

Q: Was she willing on 10.05.2025?
A: Yes, she was completely willing.